From d533d3790e057a85ffa929ecea4bf8fd77326fd1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Aubrey Bailey <aubreybailey@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 3 Sep 2026 09:11:21 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] linux-postmarketos-qcom-milos: enable NFC (S3FWRN5 driver)

The Fairphone 6 has a Samsung NFC controller on i2c1@0x27 (already
noted as a comment in the device dts) but CONFIG_NFC was entirely
disabled. Enable it plus the mainline S3FWRN5 I2C driver, the closest
mainline match for this hardware family.

Companion devicetree patch (not in this tree - milos-fairphone-fp6.dts
lives in github.com/milos-mainline/linux) adds the actual i2c device
node with GPIO wiring taken from Fairphone published GPL sources
(nfc-devicetree repo, samsung/volcano-nfc-samsung-sec-slsi.dtsi).

Build-tested against the real v7.2.0-milos kernel source (olddefconfig
+ device tree compile), which caught two real bugs in an earlier draft
of this patch, both fixed here:
- CONFIG_NFC=y is impossible: net/nfc/Kconfig has
  "depends on RFKILL || !RFKILL", and RFKILL=m elsewhere in this
  defconfig, which caps NFC at =m. olddefconfig silently downgrades an
  impossible =y to =m rather than erroring, so this only surfaces by
  actually checking the resulting .config, not by reading the diff.
- CONFIG_NFC_S3FWRN5_I2C depends on NFC_NCI && I2C. NFC_NCI was not
  enabled, so the whole option was invisible and silently dropped by
  olddefconfig along with CONFIG_NFC_S3FWRN5 (only reachable via
  S3FWRN5_I2Cs select). Added CONFIG_NFC_NCI=m.

Device tree compiles clean (0 warnings/errors) against the patched
DTS. Driver module compile (drivers/nfc/s3fwrn5) not yet verified -
hit an unrelated asm-offsets.h generation issue in this build
environment, orthogonal to this patch (pre-existing upstream code,
not touched here).

UNVERIFIED: exact chip generation - vendor driver config filenames
reference "rn4v", suggesting a newer Samsung NFC IC than S3FWRN5.
Needs real-hardware testing to confirm protocol compatibility.
---
 .../config-postmarketos-qcom-milos.aarch64                   | 5 ++++-
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/device/testing/linux-postmarketos-qcom-milos/config-postmarketos-qcom-milos.aarch64 b/device/testing/linux-postmarketos-qcom-milos/config-postmarketos-qcom-milos.aarch64
index d18ea43..bb64e64 100644
--- a/device/testing/linux-postmarketos-qcom-milos/config-postmarketos-qcom-milos.aarch64
+++ b/device/testing/linux-postmarketos-qcom-milos/config-postmarketos-qcom-milos.aarch64
@@ -1629,7 +1629,10 @@ CONFIG_RFKILL_INPUT=y
 # CONFIG_RFKILL_GPIO is not set
 # CONFIG_NET_9P is not set
 # CONFIG_CEPH_LIB is not set
-# CONFIG_NFC is not set
+CONFIG_NFC=m
+CONFIG_NFC_NCI=m
+CONFIG_NFC_S3FWRN5=m
+CONFIG_NFC_S3FWRN5_I2C=m
 # CONFIG_PSAMPLE is not set
 # CONFIG_NET_IFE is not set
 # CONFIG_LWTUNNEL is not set
-- 
